  "body": "Goose entry for the multicore server challenge: epoll event loops, a hand-written Postgres client, and 5-lane bcrypt. Details are in `submissions/goose-epoll-xeonfx/README.md`.\r\n\r\n## Latest change: batched list reads\r\n\r\nPorted from #7 `rust-tokio-Scooter1337`, so Postgres does less work per request:\r\n- **Batched list reads.** List reads of one kind (all, tag, author, favorited) that queue while a batch is in flight go to Postgres as one statement: parameters as arrays through `unnest(...) WITH ORDINALITY`, each member's page in a `LATERAL`, rows routed back by member number. A quiet server sends reads at once. The feed is never batched.\r\n- **Articles read once.** When at least half the members ask for the same page, each article's tags, favorite count and author are read once per batch; `favorited` and `following` stay per member.\r\n- **`GET /api/tags`** reads waiting together share one execution.\r\n- **SQL.** Global and tag lists read favorite count and `favorited` in one scan of the favorites; the favorited list and comments read the viewer's favorites and followees once; creating an article inserts only missing tags.\r\n- New settings: `READ_BATCH` (32; 0 turns batching off) and `READ_HOLD` (1).\r\n\r\n## How it was checked\r\n\r\n- All 197 conformance steps pass.\r\n- A concurrent check sends the same 6,000 list and tags reads to a batched server and to one with `READ_BATCH=0` on the same database: no answer differs, and every batch form runs. With the row routing broken on purpose, 253 answers differ.\r\n\r\n## Results (c4-highcpu-8, fresh full seed, 60 s ramp, 60 s measured, load from two c4-highcpu-8)\r\n\r\n| Users | Build | req/s | p95 ms | p99 ms | Errors | CPU app / Postgres | Verdict |\r\n|--:|---|--:|--:|--:|--:|---|---|\r\n| 120,000 | before | 31,841 | 6.1 | 11.8 | 0 | 18% / 76% | pass |\r\n| 120,000 | now | 31,770 | 3.7 | 6.7 | 0 | 18% / 72% | pass |\r\n| 130,000 | before | 34,052 | 177 | 240 | 0 | 18% / 80% | pass |\r\n| 130,000 | now | 34,486 | 6.0 | 9.8 | 0 | 19% / 75% | pass |\r\n| 140,000 | before | 34,143 | 623 | 742 | 0 | 19% / 80% | fails p95 |\r\n| 140,000 | now | 36,996 | 10.1 | 21.2 | 0 | 19% / 77% | pass |\r\n| 150,000 | before | 34,074 | 951 | 1,076 | 0 | 20% / 79% | fails p95, p99 |\r\n| 150,000 | now | 39,653 | 20.3 | 55.6 | 0 | 20% / 77% | pass |\r\n| 160,000 | now | 41,249 | 368 | 501 | 0 | 22% / 77% | pass |\r\n| 175,000 | now | 41,500 | 967 | 2,818 | 0 | 23% / 76% | fails p95, p99 |\r\n\r\nNot tested before merge: 5-minute holds of the new build, and the scored run's warm-up on a database that has grown.\r\n",
